      "text": "Modern drama (roughly 1870–1960) is defined by successive rejections: naturalism rejected romantic melodrama; expressionism rejected naturalism; Brecht rejected Aristotelian empathy; the Absurdists rejected logical plot progression. Each new form is a response to the failure of the previous one to capture \"the truth\" of human experience in a world after Darwin, Freud, Marx, and two World Wars."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-MODERN-DRAMA.md#003",
      "path": [
        "04-MODERN-DRAMA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:04-modern-drama, git-history:theater-performance:04-modern-drama]",
