        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Modern Drama",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nSTRINDBERG — TWO PHASES\n------------------------\nNATURALIST PHASE:\n  Miss Julie (1888): class and sex as forces destroying\n  both characters. Stage directions insist on maximum\n  naturalism: no intermission, no painted flats, real\n  props, kitchen as setting, complete psychological\n  motivation.\n  The preface is a manifesto for naturalist drama."
    }
